      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "NAMASTE (1) gave away a big start on the bend then closed in good style to be beaten under two lengths over 1500m at Kembla last start. Competitive in Sydney Saturday company last prep so this type of race is well within reach. Blinkers back on a strong sign from the Baker camp that he is ready to fire. VIVA MAURICIO (5) failed on a heavy track at Rosehill recently after a strong first-up win at Hawkesbury. Can bounce back on firmer footing. GLISSANDO (7) dominated at Kembla last start at just her second appearance. Must be respected with J Mac in the irons. SALOON PASSAGE (3) raced at Rosehill on Saturday and struggled in a BM72 over 1500m. Maiden winner the run before at midweek level. Capable of a better effort today. The other runners make little appeal.",
